==German==

===Pronunciation===
*{{audio|De-at-bekommen.ogg|audio (Austria)}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-strong|bekommt|bekam|bekommen|auxiliary=both}}

# {{transitive|auxiliary: “[[haben]]”}} to [[receive]]; to [[get]]
#: ''Hunger '''bekommen''''' — “to feel hungry” (Literally, “to get hunger”)
#: ''ein Kind '''bekommen''''' — “to have a child”
# {{transitive|auxiliary: “[[haben]]”}} to [[catch]]
# {{intransitive|with a dative case object|of food or drink|lang=de|auxiliary: “[[sein]]”}} to [[agree]] with (someone); to [[sit]] well with (someone)
#: ''Das Essen '''bekommt''' ihm nicht.'' — “The food does not agree with him.”

